  "preamble": "Deaffrication of the lateral affricate [tɬ] to [t] characterizes the southern and eastern periphery of Nahuan. The affricate arose in Proto-Nahuan from Uto-Aztecan *t before *a (Whorf's law), so the t of Pochutec, Pipil and Sierra de Puebla Nahuatl is a secondary innovation: Classical Nahuatl metlatl 'metate' and cōlōtl 'scorpion' correspond to Pipil metat and kulut, with both root tl and the absolutive suffix -tl reduced to t.",
